level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Enterprises</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Optimize large-scale campaigns</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Maximize profitability</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Best Practices for Amazon Advertising Success</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To get the most out of <strong><a href=\"https://www.tech2globe.com/amazon-marketing-services\">amazon marketing services</a></strong>, follow these tips:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Focus on high-intent keywords</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Continuously optimize campaigns</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Monitor performance metrics</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Use a mix of ad types</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Invest in professional management</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Amazon Marketing Improves Business Growth</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>With the right strategy, Amazon advertising can:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Increase product visibility</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Drive targeted traffic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Boost conversions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Improve brand recognition</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Deliver measurable ROI</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It’s not just advertising—it’s a <strong>growth engine for your eCommerce business</strong>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Get Started with Tech2Globe Today</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you want to:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Increase Amazon sales</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Improve ad performance</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Reduce wasted ad spend</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Scale your eCommerce business</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Partner with Tech2Globe’s Amazon marketing experts today and unlock your brand’s full potential.</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>FAQ Section (People Also Ask)</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. What are Amazon Marketing Services?</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Amazon Marketing Services is an advertising platform that helps sellers promote products through sponsored ads and targeted campaigns.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. How much does Amazon advertising cost?</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Costs depend on your bidding strategy, competition, and campaign setup. You only pay when users click your ads.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Is Amazon PPC worth it?</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes, when optimized correctly, Amazon PPC delivers high ROI by targeting high-intent buyers.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. Can I manage Amazon ads myself?</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes, but it requires expertise, time, and constant monitoring. Many businesses prefer outsourcing for better results.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. How does Tech2Globe help with Amazon marketing?</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tech2Globe provides end-to-end campaign management, optimization, and strategy to maximize ROI and sales growth.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','https://blog.tech2globe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Tech2globe-Blog-Banners-NEw-4.jpg','publish','Tech2globe',1,'2026-03-31 14:38:42','2026-06-01 11:30:26','2026-06-01 11:30:26'),(12,'Is Power BI a Business Intelligence Tool?','is-power-bi-a-business-intelligence-tool','','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’ve been looking into data tools, you’ve probably seen Microsoft Power BI everywhere and thought okay, but is this actually a business intelligence tool or just another fancy dashboard thing?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Short answer: yes, it <em>is</em> a business intelligence tool.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But that answer only makes sense when you look at how people actually use it inside a business.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What People Think vs What It Actually Does</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A lot of people assume Power BI is just for making charts. That’s usually because the first thing you see is dashboards.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But dashboards are just the surface.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The real job of a business intelligence tool is to take messy, scattered data and make it useful enough for someone to make a decision without overthinking it. That’s the part most tools fail at.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI actually handles that part pretty well.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Where It Starts Feeling Like a BI Tool</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Think about a typical situation.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Your marketing data is in one place, sales data is somewhere else, and finance has their own numbers. If you want a proper view of the business, you either ask three different people or try to combine everything manually.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That’s where Power BI starts behaving like a real BI tool.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It pulls everything into one place, and once you see all the numbers together, things stop feeling confusing. You’re not guessing anymore you’re connecting the dots.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads:</strong> <a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/how-to-calculate-business-days-in-power-bi/\">How to Calculate Business Days in Power BI (Without Overcomplicating It)</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>It’s Not Just Showing Data, It’s Helping You Think</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is the main difference.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A reporting tool will show you what happened. A business intelligence tool helps you understand what to do next.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>With Power BI, you’re not just looking at numbers. You’re spotting patterns.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You notice things like:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>which campaigns are actually bringing revenue</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>where sales are slowing down</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>what’s eating into your margins</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And once you see that clearly, decisions become easier. You don’t need long discussions or back-and-forth explanations.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why Businesses Actually Use It</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most companies don’t adopt Power BI because it looks good. They use it because they’re tired of unclear reporting.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At some point, spreadsheets stop working. Reports take too long. Teams start arguing over whose numbers are correct.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI fixes a lot of that by giving everyone the same view.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When everyone is looking at the same data, decisions stop being debates and start becoming actions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads:</strong> <a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/how-does-power-bi-help-in-making-business/\">How Does Power BI Help in Making Business Decisions? (From a Practical Business Perspective)</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Where It’s Different From Basic Tools</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A lot of tools can generate reports. That’s not special.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>What makes Power BI different is how flexible it is.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You can dig deeper into the data, filter things, compare performance, and explore without needing someone else to rebuild a report for you every time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That freedom is what makes it feel like a proper business intelligence setup, not just a reporting system.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>So, Is Power BI Actually a BI Tool?</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes but not because of the label.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It’s because of what it allows you to do.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If a tool helps you:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>bring data together</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>understand what’s happening</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>and decide what to do next</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>then it’s doing the job of business intelligence.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI checks those boxes in a way that most businesses can actually use without building a whole data team.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads:</strong> <a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/benefits-of-power-bi-for-business/\">Benefits of Power BI for Business: Why US Companies Are Moving Toward Smarter Data</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Thought</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’re still relying on scattered reports and manual tracking, anything will feel better.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But once you start using something like Microsoft Power BI properly, you realize the difference isn’t just in the tool, it’s in how quickly you can think and act.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And that’s really what business intelligence is about.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you\'re serious about using data to grow, our <a href=\"https://www.tech2globe.com/microsoft-power-bi-consulting-services\">Power BI solutions</a> can help you build a system that drives faster, smarter decisions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','https://blog.tech2globe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Power-BI-a-Business-Intelligence-Tool.png','publish','Tech2globe',1,'2026-03-31 08:12:04','2026-06-01 11:30:26','2026-06-01 11:30:26'),(13,'How to Calculate Business Days in Power BI (Without Overcomplicating It)','how-to-calculate-business-days-in-power-bi','','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’ve ever tried to calculate business days in Microsoft Power BI, you probably realized one thing quickly, it’s not as straightforward as it sounds.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Dates are easy. But once you say “exclude weekends” or “ignore holidays,” things get tricky.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The good news is, Power BI can handle this well you just need the right approach.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>First, What Do We Mean by Business Days?</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Before jumping into formulas, let’s be clear.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Business days usually mean:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Monday to Friday</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>excluding weekends</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>optionally excluding holidays</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>So if you’re calculating things like:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>delivery timelines</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>project durations</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>SLA tracking</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You need a way to count only working days between two dates.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Create or Use a Date Table (Very Important)</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’re not already using a date table, this is where most people go wrong.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In Power BI, you should always have a proper calendar table. It gives you full control over dates.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A simple date table looks like this:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>DateTable =</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>ADDCOLUMNS (</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALENDAR (DATE(2023,1,1), DATE(2026,12,31)),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\"DayOfWeek\", WEEKDAY([Date], 2),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\"IsWeekend\", IF(WEEKDAY([Date], 2) &gt; 5, TRUE(), FALSE())</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>What this does:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>creates a full calendar</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>marks weekends clearly</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Now you have a foundation to work with.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Exclude Weekends</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Once your date table is ready, calculating business days becomes easier.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Let’s say you have:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Start Date</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>End Date</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You can count business days like this:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Business Days =</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>CALCULATE(</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;COUNTROWS(\'DateTable\'),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\'DateTable\'[Date] &gt;= MIN(\'Table\'[Start Date]),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\'DateTable\'[Date] &lt;= MAX(\'Table\'[End Date]),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\'DateTable\'[IsWeekend] = FALSE()</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This basically:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>filters dates between start and end</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>removes weekends</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>counts remaining days</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That’s your working days.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads: </strong><a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/benefits-of-power-bi-for-business/\">Benefits of Power BI for Business: Why US Companies Are Moving Toward Smarter Data</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Exclude Holidays (Optional but Important)</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In real business scenarios, weekends aren’t enough. You also need to remove holidays.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For this, create a <strong>Holiday Table</strong>, something like:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>HolidayTable =</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>DATATABLE(</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\"Date\", DATE,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{DATE(2026,1,1)},</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{DATE(2026,12,25)}</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Then update your calculation:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Business Days =</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>CALCULATE(</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;COUNTROWS(\'DateTable\'),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\'DateTable\'[Date] &gt;= MIN(\'Table\'[Start Date]),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\'DateTable\'[Date] &lt;= MAX(\'Table\'[End Date]),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\'DateTable\'[IsWeekend] = FALSE(),</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NOT \'DateTable\'[Date] IN VALUES(\'HolidayTable\'[Date])</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Now you\'re excluding both:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>weekends</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>holidays</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is how most companies actually calculate business days.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: When You Need It Row by Row</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you want to calculate business days per row (like per order or ticket), use a measure carefully with row context or create a calculated column depending on your use case.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In most cases, measures work better because they stay dynamic.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Common Mistakes to Avoid</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is where people usually mess up:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>1. Not using a date table</strong><strong><br></strong> Trying to calculate directly from raw dates creates issues later.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>2. Ignoring holidays</strong><strong><br></strong> Your numbers look correct, but business-wise they’re wrong.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>3. Using simple date difference</strong><strong><br></strong> DATEDIFF counts all days, not business days.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads: </strong><a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/how-does-power-bi-help-in-making-business/\">How Does Power BI Help in Making Business Decisions? (From a Practical Business Perspective)</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>When This Actually Matters in Business</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This isn’t just a technical thing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Calculating business days properly helps in:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>tracking delivery timelines</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>measuring team performance</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>managing SLAs</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>forecasting project completion</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If this calculation is wrong, your decisions based on it will also be off.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Thought</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Calculating business days in Microsoft Power BI is not complicated once you structure it correctly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The key is simple:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>build a proper date table</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>mark weekends</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>exclude holidays when needed</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Once that’s in place, everything else becomes straightforward.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Need help implementing this in your business? Our <a href=\"https://www.tech2globe.com/microsoft-power-bi-consulting-services\">Power BI experts</a> can build scalable, real-world dashboards for you.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','https://blog.tech2globe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/How-to-Calculate-Business-Days-in-Power-BI-Without-Overcomplicating-It.png','publish','Tech2globe',1,'2026-03-29 08:01:25','2026-06-01 11:30:26','2026-06-01 11:30:26'),(14,'Power BI for Small Business: When It Actually Starts Making Sense','power-bi-for-small-business','','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most small business owners don’t wake up thinking, “I need a business intelligence tool.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>What usually happens is slower than that.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At first, everything runs on simple systems. A few spreadsheets, maybe some reports from your ad platforms, basic numbers from your accountant. It works… until it doesn’t.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You reach a point where the numbers are there, but clarity is missing. You’re looking at data, but still asking questions like “What’s actually working?” or “Where is the money going?”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That’s usually the stage where tools like Microsoft Power BI start becoming relevant for small businesses.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why “Power BI for Small Business” Even Comes Up</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The idea of power bi for small business doesn’t come up in the early days.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It shows up when things get slightly complex.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Maybe you’re running ads on multiple platforms. Maybe sales are coming from different channels. Maybe your expenses are growing and you want tighter control.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Individually, everything makes sense. But together, it starts feeling messy.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You’re not lacking data you’re lacking a clear view.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads: </strong><a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/benefits-of-power-bi-for-business/\">Benefits of Power BI for Business: Why US Companies Are Moving Toward Smarter Data</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Real Problem Isn’t Tools, It’s Fragmentation</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most small businesses already use multiple tools.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You’ve got:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>marketing dashboards</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>sales systems</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>payment or accounting software</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The problem is, none of them really talk to each other in a useful way.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>So when you try to make a decision, you’re jumping between tabs, comparing numbers manually, or asking different people for updates.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That’s where microsoft power bi for small business starts to feel less like a “nice-to-have” and more like something practical.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It brings everything into one place so you’re not stitching together information every time you need clarity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What Actually Changes When You Start Using It</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The biggest change is not the dashboard. It’s how you think.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Instead of asking, “Can someone send me the numbers?”, you already have them.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Instead of guessing which campaign is working, you can see it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Instead of reviewing performance once a week, you can check it anytime.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It removes friction. And in business, even small friction slows down decisions more than people realize.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads:</strong> <a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/how-does-power-bi-help-in-making-business/\">How Does Power BI Help in Making Business Decisions? (From a Practical Business Perspective)</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>It’s Not Just for “Big Companies” Anymore</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>There’s this old assumption that tools like Power BI are only for large organizations with data teams.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That’s not really true anymore.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes, big companies use it. But small businesses benefit just as much—sometimes even more—because they need to move faster and can’t afford wrong decisions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The difference is in how you use it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A small business doesn’t need complex models. Even a simple setup that shows sales, marketing, and expenses clearly can make a noticeable difference.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Where It Helps the Most (Real Situations)</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You don’t need to think in terms of features. Think in terms of everyday situations.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For example, if you’re spending money on ads, you want to know which platform is actually bringing revenue, not just clicks.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’re selling multiple products or services, you want to know which ones are worth focusing on.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If your costs are increasing, you want to see where the money is going without digging through reports.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is where power bi for small business becomes useful—not as a technical tool, but as something that answers basic business questions faster.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads:</strong> <a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/how-to-calculate-business-days-in-power-bi/\">How to Calculate Business Days in Power BI (Without Overcomplicating It)</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Only Part That Feels Hard</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To be honest, the hardest part is not using Power BI. It’s setting it up properly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You need to connect your data, structure it in a clean way, and build dashboards that actually reflect how your business works.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Once that part is done, using it becomes routine.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You open it, you check numbers, and you move on with decisions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>When You Probably Don’t Need It Yet</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It’s also important to say this clearly not every small business needs it immediately.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If your operations are still simple, with limited data and straightforward decisions, spreadsheets can still work fine.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But the moment you start feeling like your numbers are scattered or decisions are taking longer than they should, that’s usually the signal.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads:</strong> <a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/is-power-bi-a-business-intelligence-tool/\">Is Power BI a Business Intelligence Tool?</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Thought</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI for small business is not about using advanced technology. It’s about reducing confusion.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When your business grows, complexity naturally increases. The way you handle that complexity decides how smoothly you scale.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tools like Microsoft Power BI don’t magically grow your business, but they do make it easier to understand what’s happening inside it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And once you have that clarity, decisions stop feeling heavy. They just become part of the process.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','https://blog.tech2globe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Power-BI-for-Small-Business.png','publish','Tech2globe',1,'2026-03-28 08:26:19','2026-06-01 11:30:27','2026-06-01 11:30:27'),(15,'What is Shopify Theme Development (And Why Your Store Actually Needs It)','what-is-shopify-theme-development','','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Let’s be real for a second. Anyone can sign up for Shopify, grab a free template, and have a store live by dinner time. But if you’re trying to build a serious brand in the US market, looking like a carbon copy of ten thousand other drop-shippers is eventually going to hurt your sales.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You inevitably hit a wall. You want a very specific layout for your product pages, a lightning-fast checkout flow, or a custom feature that a generic plug-and-play app just can\'t fix. That’s usually the exact moment founders start asking: <em>what is Shopify theme development</em>, and is it actually worth the cash?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Here is the no-nonsense breakdown of what it means, why templates eventually fail you, and why outsourcing this work is the ultimate growth hack.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Getting Under the Hood</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At its core, Shopify theme development isn\'t just changing your button colors or swapping out a logo. It’s the process of building a custom storefront from the ground up, or heavily modifying an existing one at the code level.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Instead of fighting with a rigid drag-and-drop editor, developers dive into Shopify’s unique coding language (called Liquid), along with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. They are literally architecting how your store behaves and feels to the customer.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Problem With \"App Bloat\"</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Free or cheap premium themes are totally fine for your first few months. But as you scale, they get incredibly clunky. You end up installing twenty different third-party apps just to get the basic features you want.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The result? Bloated code and a sluggish site. In the US, if your site takes more than three seconds to load, the buyer is already hitting the back button and heading to Amazon. Custom development strips away the junk. You get exactly the features you need built natively into the theme, meaning blazing fast speeds and a user experience that feels premium. It’s the difference between renting a generic apartment and building a custom home.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The SEO Elephant in the Room</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You can\'t talk about web design without talking about traffic. A lot of store owners panic when they think about messing with their site\'s structure. If you’ve ever wondered, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=https://blog.tech2globe.com/is-shopify-good-for-seo/\">is Shopify good for SEO?</a>, the answer is a massive yes—but only if the underlying code is clean. A custom-developed theme is built with search engines in mind from day one.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But here\'s the catch: if you already have an established store, you have to tread lightly. Ripping out your old design and slapping on a new one without a game plan can absolutely tank your rankings. You need to understand exactly how <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=https://blog.tech2globe.com/changing-shopify-themes-seo/\">changing Shopify themes impacts your SEO</a> before you touch anything. We\'re talking proper redirects, preserved metadata, and zero broken links.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The In-House Trap vs. The Outsourcing Hack</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>So, who actually builds this for you? Trying to learn custom code while running a business is a quick way to break your checkout and lose money. But hiring an in-house developer is a massive trap for scaling brands.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Think about it: you spend weeks interviewing, negotiating a massive US salary, and paying for health benefits and software licenses. If sales dip in the summer, you\'re still locked into that hefty full-time payroll.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is exactly why smart founders decide to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=https://blog.tech2globe.com/hire-a-shopify-developer-in-the-us/\">hire a Shopify developer in the US</a> through an outsourced agency model instead. When you outsource, the entire landscape shifts:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Zero HR Headaches:</strong> You get plug-and-play expertise. No benefits to manage, no sick days to cover, just a flat, predictable rate for elite work.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Ultimate Agility:</strong> You can scale the dev team up during the Q4 holiday rush and scale them back down in January.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Speed to Market:</strong> Instead of hunting for talent for months, an agency has fully trained professionals logged in and tackling your site\'s code within days.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Outsourcing removes the friction of growth. It lets you punch way above your weight class without taking on massive financial risk.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ready to Upgrade?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Your storefront is your absolute best salesperson. If it’s slow, confusing, or looks generic, you are leaving serious money on the table.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you\'re ready to stop fighting with templates and build an e-commerce machine that actually converts, the experts at <strong><a href=\"https://tech2globe.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Tech2Globe</a></strong> have your back. As a premier <a href=\"https://www.tech2globe.com/shopify-development-company\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Shopify development company</a>, we handle the heavy lifting from custom Liquid coding to flawless SEO migrations, so you can get back to actually running your empire.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','https://blog.tech2globe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Shopify-Theme-Development.png','publish','Tech2globe',1,'2026-03-28 04:49:41','2026-06-01 11:30:27','2026-06-01 11:30:27'),(16,'How Does Power BI Help in Making Business Decisions? (From a Practical Business Perspective)','how-does-power-bi-help-in-making-business','','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you run a business or even manage a team, you already know this data is everywhere, but clarity is not.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You’ve got numbers coming in from ads, sales, CRM, finance tools… but when it’s time to actually decide something, you still end up asking people for reports or digging through Excel sheets. And half the time, by the time you get the numbers, they’re already outdated.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That’s the gap tools like Microsoft Power BI try to fix. Not by giving you “more data,” but by helping you actually understand what’s going on without wasting time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>So instead of giving you textbook benefits, here’s how Power BI actually helps in making business decisions in real-life scenarios.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. You Stop Waiting for Reports</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>One of the biggest changes you notice is this, you don’t have to wait anymore.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In most companies, someone has to prepare a report before you can even look at the numbers. With Power BI, you just open a dashboard and it’s already there, updated.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That changes how decisions happen. You’re not planning based on last week’s data. You’re reacting to what’s happening right now.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. You Finally See the Full Picture</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Normally, every team has their own data. Marketing shows one story, sales shows another, finance shows something else.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The problem is, you never really see how everything connects.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI pulls all of that into one place. And when you see everything together, decisions become a lot clearer because you’re not looking at isolated numbers anymore you’re looking at the business as a whole.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>More Reads: </strong><a href=\"https://blog.tech2globe.com/benefits-of-power-bi-for-business/\">Benefits of Power BI for Business: Why US Companies Are Moving Toward Smarter Data</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. You Don’t Need Someone to “Explain the Data”</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Let’s be honest, a lot of reports need interpretation.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You look at a spreadsheet and still have to ask, “What does this actually mean?”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI fixes that by making things visual. You don’t need someone to walk you through it. You can just look at the dashboard and understand what’s going up, what’s dropping, and what needs attention.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. You Quickly Spot What’s Working</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most businesses waste money simply because they don’t know what’s actually working.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Maybe you’re running ads on multiple platforms, or pushing different products, but you’re not 100% sure which one is really driving results.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>With Power BI, that becomes obvious. You can see performance clearly, and once you see it, decisions like “where to invest more” become much easier.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. Planning Starts Making More Sense</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A lot of business planning is guesswork, even if people don’t admit it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You look at past numbers, make some assumptions, and hope things go as expected.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI doesn’t eliminate uncertainty, but it reduces it. When you can clearly see trends and patterns, your planning becomes more grounded. You’re not just hoping you’re making informed bets.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>6. Your Team Stops Wasting Time on Manual Work</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>There’s always someone in the team stuck creating reports.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Pulling data, cleaning it, formatting it, it takes hours, sometimes days.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI automates most of that. Once it’s set up, the data flows in automatically. That frees up your team to actually think about the numbers instead of just preparing them.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>7. Marketing Decisions Become Less Risky</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’re spending money on marketing, this is where things get very real.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Without clear data, you’re basically guessing which campaign is worth scaling.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI shows you exactly what’s converting and what’s not. So instead of spreading your budget everywhere, you start focusing only on what’s bringing returns.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>8. You Get Better Control Over Finances</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Financial decisions are where mistakes hurt the most.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you don’t have a clear view of revenue, costs, and profitability, it’s easy to overspend or misallocate resources.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI gives you that visibility. You can track financial performance without waiting for end-of-month reports, which makes a big difference in how confidently you make decisions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>9. Everyone Starts Working on the Same Page</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>One hidden problem in most companies is misalignment.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Different teams use different numbers, which leads to different conclusions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI creates a shared view. Everyone looks at the same data, which means discussions become clearer and decisions become more aligned.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>10. You Move Faster Than Most Businesses</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At the end of the day, this is what it really comes down to speed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most businesses are slow because their data is slow. They take time to understand what’s happening, and by then, the opportunity is gone.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Power BI helps you move faster. You see things earlier, you react quicker, and over time, that speed adds up to a serious advantage.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Thought</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>So, how does Power BI help in making business decisions?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It doesn’t magically “fix” your business. What it does is remove the friction between data and decisions. It makes things clearer, faster, and easier to act on.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And once you start operating with that kind of clarity, you realize how much time and opportunity you were losing before.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you’re looking to set this up for your business, explore our <a href=\"https://www.tech2globe.com/microsoft-power-bi-consulting-services\">Power BI services </a>to get started the right way.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','https://blog.tech2globe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/How-Does-Power-BI-Help-in-Making-Business-Decisions.png','publish','Tech2globe',1,'2026-03-27 05:48:26','2026-06-01 11:30:27','2026-06-01 11:30:27'),(17,'How Tech2Globe Helped Businesses Discover Growth Opportunities at IndiaSoft','how-tech2globe-helped-businesses-discover-growth-opportunities-at-indiasoft','','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In today’s competitive global market, businesses need more than just ideas—they need <strong>data-driven strategies, expert execution, and scalable solutions</strong>. Events like <em>IndiaSoft</em> provide a powerful platform for companies to explore partnerships, technologies, and growth strategies.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At this prestigious industry event, <strong>Tech2Globe</strong> played a key role in helping businesses uncover new revenue streams, optimize operations, and scale effectively.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This blog explores how <strong>Tech2Globe IndiaSoft growth opportunities</strong> translated into real business impact across industries.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why IndiaSoft Matters for Global Business Growth</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>IndiaSoft is one of the leading platforms where global buyers and Indian service providers connect. It brings together:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Technology innovators</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Digital service providers</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Startups and enterprises</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Global decision-makers</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For businesses, it’s not just about networking—it’s about <strong>finding actionable growth strategies</strong>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is where Tech2Globe stands out.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Tech2Globe Delivered Value at IndiaSoft</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tech2Globe didn’t just participate—they <strong>actively helped businesses solve real challenges</strong>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Identifying Untapped Growth Opportunities</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Many businesses struggle to identify where growth actually lies.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tech2Globe helped companies:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Analyze market gaps</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Discover new customer segments</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Identify profitable channels</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Build scalable expansion strategies</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Real Use Case:</strong><strong><br></strong> An eCommerce brand discovered new international markets through Tech2Globe’s research insights, leading 